title: "statement-store: keep the other axis when a decrease depletes an allowance"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `decrease_allowance_by` now removes an allowance only when both axes reach zero, and
      otherwise keeps the remainder. Before, one axis reaching zero dropped the other, which
      another source may have granted, so grants and revokes from several sources had to be
      ordered. They now compose in any order.

      `get_allowance` can now return a depleted remainder, which grants no statements; use
      `StatementAllowance::is_depleted` to check. `StatementAllowance` now derives `Copy`.

crates:
  - name: sp-statement-store
    bump: minor
